{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q9NRZ7","uniProtkbId":"PLCC_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"1-acyl-sn-glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferase gamma"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21173190"}],"value":"2.3.1.51"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"1-acylglycerol-3-phosphate O-acyltransferase 3"},"shortNames":[{"value":"1-AGP acyltransferase 3"},{"value":"1-AGPAT 3"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Lysophosphatidic acid acyltransferase gamma"},"shortNames":[{"value":"LPAAT-gamma"}]}]},"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9D517"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21173190"}],"value":"Converts 1-acyl-sn-glycerol-3-phosphate (lysophosphatidic acid or LPA) into 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol-3-phosphate (phosphatidic acid or PA) by incorporating an acyl moiety at the sn-2 position of the glycerol backbone (PubMed:21173190). Acts on LPA containing saturated or unsaturated fatty acids C16:0-C20:4 at the sn-1 position using C18:1, C20:4 or C18:2-CoA as the acyl donor (PubMed:21173190). Also acts on lysophosphatidylcholine, lysophosphatidylinositol and lysophosphatidylserine using C18:1 or C20:4-CoA (PubMed:21173190). Has a preference for arachidonoyl-CoA as a donor (By similarity). Also has a modest lysophosphatidylinositol acyltransferase (LPIAT) activity, converts lysophosphatidylinositol (LPI) into phosphatidylinositol (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20537980"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21173190"}],"value":"Endoplasmic reticulum membrane","id":"SL-0097"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"ev